611        /* STAT-CALIS-026: CALIS — Case-Level Residuals, Outliers, Leverage Observations, and Residual Diagnostics
612         * Source: S154 / Chapter 33 / `Case-Level Residuals, Outliers, Leverage Observations, and Residual Diagnostics` (PDF pp. 1789–1793).
613         * Discriminates: Example 33.14: Residual Diagnostics and Robust Estimation
614         */
615        options nosyntaxcheck obs=max firstobs=1 nodate nonumber nocenter linesize=160 pagesize=max nostimer nofullstimer validvarname=v7
615      ! validmemname=compatible locale=en_US;
616        %let syscc=0;
617        title; footnote;
618        ods _all_ close;
619        ods listing gpath="%sysfunc(pathname(work))";
620        ods graphics off;
621        proc datasets library=work kill nolist;
NOTE: Deleting WORK.REGION1 (memtype=DATA).
NOTE: Deleting WORK.REGION2 (memtype=DATA).
NOTE: Deleting WORK.REGSTRY (memtype=ITEMSTOR).
NOTE: File WORK.REGSTRY (memtype=ITEMSTOR) cannot be deleted because it is in use.
NOTE: Deleting WORK.SASGOPT (memtype=CATALOG).
NOTE: File WORK.SASGOPT (memtype=CATALOG) cannot be deleted because it is in use.
NOTE: Deleting WORK.SASMAC1 (memtype=CATALOG).
NOTE: File WORK.SASMAC1 (memtype=CATALOG) cannot be deleted because it is in use.
NOTE: Deleting WORK.WHEATON (memtype=DATA).
621      !                                         quit;


622        ods path work.templat(update) sashelp.tmplmst(read);
623        
624        data mardia;
625        call streaminit(314159);
626        do id=1 to 120;
627         fact=rand('normal');
628         mechanics=60+8*fact+4*rand('normal');
629         vector=65+7*fact+4*rand('normal');
630         algebra=63+9*fact+4*rand('normal');
631         analysis=64+6*fact+4*rand('normal');
632         statistics=66+8*fact+4*rand('normal');
633         if id=120 then mechanics=mechanics+30;
634         output;
635        end;
636        drop fact id;
637        run;

NOTE: The data set WORK.MARDIA has 120 observations and 5 variables.

638        ods graphics on;
639        proc calis data=mardia residual plots=caseresid;
640        path
641        fact1 ===> mechanics vector algebra analysis statistics = 1. ;
642        run;

NOTE: The parameter list is shorter than the path list that contains fact1 ===> vector in the PATH statement. The path fact1 ===> vector and all the remaining 
      paths are free parameters.
NOTE: Convergence criterion (GCONV=1E-8) satisfied.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE CALIS printed pages 72-83.

643        ods graphics off;
644        ods graphics on;
645        proc calis data=mardia residual robust plots=caseresid pcorr;
646        path
647        fact1 ===> mechanics vector algebra analysis statistics = 1. ;
648        run;

NOTE: The parameter list is shorter than the path list that contains fact1 ===> vector in the PATH statement. The path fact1 ===> vector and all the remaining 
      paths are free parameters.
NOTE: Saturated mean structures in models are analyzed with the ROBUST or ROBUST=RESID option.
NOTE: The robust mean and covariance matrices with the 2-stage robust method are obtained successfully in 10 iterations.
NOTE: The leverage M-Distances are computed by using the results of the 2-stage robust method.
NOTE: Robust estimation with the iteratively reweighted least squares method converges in 11 iterations.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE CALIS printed pages 84-95.

649        ods graphics off;
650        proc calis data=mardia robust=sat pcorr;
651        path
652        fact1 ===> mechanics vector algebra analysis statistics = 1. ;
653        run;

NOTE: The parameter list is shorter than the path list that contains fact1 ===> vector in the PATH statement. The path fact1 ===> vector and all the remaining 
      paths are free parameters.
NOTE: The robust mean and covariance matrices with the 2-stage robust method are obtained successfully in 10 iterations.
NOTE: Convergence criterion (ABSGCONV=0.00001) satisfied.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE CALIS printed pages 96-103.

